      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. As written, it's a dose that could harm the patient.\n\n- **Single dose:** 1600 mg is above the usual maximum single prescription dose of ibuprofen, which is 800 mg. Higher single doses add little pain relief and increase side effects.\n- **Daily total:** 1600 mg four times daily is 6400 mg/day. The labeled maximum for adults is 3200 mg/day, even for chronic conditions, and most inpatient use is far lower.\n\nThe patient's normal kidney and liver function and the absence of allergies don't change this. The main risks at this dose are GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events.\n\nMedication orders also need to come from a licensed prescriber, so this should go to the medicine team regardless of the dose. A prescriber should confirm the intended dose, which may be something like 400\u2013800 mg per dose with a maximum of 3200 mg/day, and the indication. Once a prescriber gives me the corrected dose and frequency, I can enter it."
      }
     ],
